[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Apostrophe Not Quoting
Comment=Two apostrophes that happen to BALANCE. A naive shell parser would read
Comment[x-note]="'s a b'" as a quoted region and silently produce "its a bs".
Comment[x-note2]=Neither opening quote sits at an argument boundary, so the
Comment[x-note3]=compatibility pattern must NOT be recognised here and the strict
Comment[x-note4]=grammar, which is correct for apostrophes, must be kept.
Exec=/usr/bin/apostrophe --msg it's a b's
Icon=apostrophe
Terminal=false
